The summer months are over, and it is time to get the GL Masonic Youth
Committee together again. Our first meeting will be held this coming Monday
night, September 7, at 6:00 pm via Zoom. Since our meeting nights are held
on the first Mondays of each month, the September meeting is always on Labor
Day. We need to hold the meeting anyway, Hopefully, if you are traveling
that weekend, you can be back home in time for the call. Please let me know
if you are unable to attend.

 

Please welcome WB Michael Fluty, Junior Grand Deacon, who will be serving as
our Observer this term. We actually prefer that he not only observe but
contribute to our discussions as needed. Welcome WB Michael!

 

Please bring any upcoming youth events to the attention of the Committee at
this meeting. In addition, we need to review the 2025 Goals & Objectives we
submitted a year ago. Please take a look at these prior to our meeting and
be ready to discuss, propose changes, or whatever is needed to make them
applicable to what we want to accomplish this Masonic term. As in the past,
I only have the free version of Zoom, so our meeting will be limited to 40
minutes or less.

 

The ID and password for the Zoom meeting remain the same and are included
below for your convenience.

https://us04web.zoom.us/j/5561132706 

password: glmyc2020

Fraternally,

Alan Dye

 


